  "overview": "**Blade** is a light-first design system anchored on `#f5f5f5` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (18.0:1 contrast) and `hsla(218, 89%, 51%, 1)` brand accent.\n\nDisplay headlines pair `Inter` with `System UI` body copy (40px display down to 16px body), unified by `4px` base corner radius and stepped `#f5f5f5` -> `hsla(0, 0%, 97%, 1)` surface layering.\n\nMaintained by **Razorpay**. Source: published token package (https://github.com/razorpay/blade), repo https://github.com/razorpay/blade. Inventory: **90** colors, **22** typography steps, and **13** documented components (see repository license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 13 component tokens with documented paddings: `12px 20px`, `0`, `16px`, `1px 3px`, `8px 12px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `hsla(0, 0%, 97%, 1)` cards; separate sibling sections using `hsla(204, 8%, 88%, 1)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Surface & Stroke Elevation**: Relies on crisp tonal contrast (`#f5f5f5` -> `hsla(0, 0%, 97%, 1)`) and `1px solid hsla(204, 8%, 88%, 1)` hairlines instead of heavy drop shadows.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `hsla(218, 89%, 51%, 1)` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#f5f5f5` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `hsla(218, 89%, 51%, 1)` with `#f7f7f8` text (4.8:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `Inter` headings with `System UI` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `4px` base geometry across inputs and buttons (4px on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `hsla(0, 0%, 97%, 1)` surface shifts and `hsla(204, 8%, 88%, 1)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `4px` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input` fields and secondary buttons."
}
